# EUVisaAdvice Academy - Frontend Rules

Scope: frontend only. No backend, API, or database work unless explicitly requested.

## Stack (planned, from `gemini.md` and the sibling `euvisaadvice` app)
- Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS v4.
- Path alias `@/*` -> `./src/*`.
- `euacademy/` has no app code yet. When scaffolding, confirm the stack with the user, then follow these rules and the framework defaults.
- Do not add dependencies without a clear need. Tell the user when you add one.

## 1. Coding standards
- TypeScript everywhere. No `any` (use `unknown` + narrowing, or proper types). No `@ts-ignore` without a comment explaining why.
- Naming: components/types `PascalCase`; hooks `useThing`; functions/variables `camelCase`; constants `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`; component files `PascalCase.tsx`; non-component files and route folders `kebab-case`.
- Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only when state, effects, or browser APIs are needed, and push it to the smallest leaf component.
- Handle loading, empty, and error states for every data-driven view (`loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx` where it fits).
- Use `next/image`, `next/link`, and `next/font` instead of raw `<img>`, `<a>`, and font links.
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, labels for inputs, visible focus states, alt text, keyboard-operable controls.
- Keep it simple. No speculative abstractions, no dead code, no commented-out code, no stray `console.log`.

## 2. Project structure (`src/`)
```
src/
  app/                  # routes, layouts, loading/error files only; keep pages thin
    (marketing)/        # public: marketplace, course details, sales page
    (student)/          # dashboard, lesson players, quiz, payment success
    (studio)/           # admin: dashboard, courses, curriculum builder, uploads, students
  components/
    ui/                 # primitives: Button, Card, Input, Badge, Accordion, ProgressBar
    layout/             # Navbar, Footer, Sidebar, page shells
    <feature>/          # course/, player/, quiz/, studio/ ... feature-specific components
  hooks/                # reusable hooks
  lib/                  # utilities and helpers (pure functions)
  services/             # data access / API client wrappers (mock data lives here until a backend exists)
  types/                # shared TypeScript types
  constants/            # shared constants and config
  styles/               # global CSS and theme tokens
public/                 # static assets
```
- Route groups and folder names are suggestions. Follow Next.js conventions and keep nesting shallow.
- UI components must not fetch data or hold business logic. Put that in hooks, `services/`, or server code.
- Co-locate a component's private subcomponents/types with it. Move anything used by 2+ features to `components/ui` or `components/<shared>`.

## 3. Component reusability
- Before creating a component, search `src/components` for one to reuse or extend (props, variants, composition, `children`).
- One component per file, with a single, focused responsibility. Never define several independent components in one file.
- Single source of truth: fix or change a shared component in its original file. Never copy it, fork it per page, or patch it locally.
- Create a page-specific variant only when the requirements genuinely differ. Prefer a `variant` or `size` prop first.
- Repeated UI (cards, stat tiles, lesson rows, status badges, tables, form fields) must be a shared component.

## 4. File size
- Keep every source file under 300 lines (a ceiling, not a target).
- Near the limit, extract components, hooks, utilities, types, or constants.
- Go over only when splitting would hurt readability or break a framework convention. Add a short comment at the top of the file explaining why.
- Don't split into tiny files for the sake of it.

## 5. Stitch designs are the source of truth
- Stitch project: `projects/14608643000741593592` ("Legal Course Platform UI"), https://stitch.withgoogle.com/projects/14608643000741593592
- Stitch MCP server `stitch` is configured in `.cursor/mcp.json` (local only, gitignored; never commit the API key).
- Before building any screen: fetch its screen, screenshot, and HTML/code from Stitch via the MCP (`list_screens`, `get_screen`) and inspect it. Do not work from memory.
- Match the design pixel-for-pixel: layout, dimensions, spacing, padding, margins, typography, font weights, colors, borders, shadows, radii, alignment, icon placement, image proportions.
- Do not invent UI, change layouts, or swap in generic components when Stitch specifies the look.
- Preserve the design across breakpoints (mobile, tablet, desktop). Where Stitch only shows desktop, follow the design system's mobile tokens (`display-hero-mobile`, `margin-mobile`, ...) and say what you assumed.
- If a detail is unclear or an asset is missing, stop and flag it. Do not guess.
- Known screens (all desktop): Courses Marketplace; Course Details & Sales Page; Course Overview & Curriculum; Student Dashboard - My Learning; Video Lesson Player; Text & Audio Lesson Player; Knowledge-Check Quiz; Payment Success; Studio: Admin Dashboard & Analytics, Course Management & Catalog, Create New Course, Curriculum Builder & Lesson Editor, Topic-Wise Video Upload, Student Management & Transactions; plus the overall "Academy & Studio Management System" overview.

### Design tokens ("Sovereign Legal Academy", dark theme)
Re-read the full design system from Stitch (`get_project` -> `designTheme.designMd`) when in doubt. Core values:
- Font: Plus Jakarta Sans (all text); JetBrains Mono for code labels. Base radius `0.5rem` (sm `0.25`, md `0.75`, lg `1`, xl `1.5`).
- Backgrounds: `surface-base #070A10`, `background #0f131c`, `surface-level-1 #111722`, `surface-level-2 #151C28`, `surface-elevated #1A2332`.
- Gold: `primary-container #D9A441`, `gold-hover #E4B44F`, `gold-highlight #F0C264`, `gold-hairline rgba(218,164,65,.22)`, `gold-subtle-fill rgba(217,164,65,.08)`.
- Text: `#FFFFFF` primary, `#A1A7B4` secondary, `#6B7280` muted. Border: `#222B3A`.
- Status: success `#10B981`, warning `#F59E0B`, danger `#EF4444` (each with a 12% background).
- Type scale: display-hero 3.5rem/800, headline-lg 2.5rem/700, headline-md 1.75rem/600, headline-sm 1.25rem/600, title-card 1.125rem/600, body-default 0.9375rem, body-muted 0.875rem, label-caps 0.6875rem/700 with 0.12em tracking.
- Spacing: gutter 1.5rem, margin 2rem (desktop 3rem, mobile 1rem), steps 0.25 / 0.5 / 0.75 / 1 / 1.5 / 2 / 3 / 4rem.
- Borders are 1px, except the active curriculum rail (`3px solid #D9A441`).

## 6. Styling
- Tailwind v4 utilities with design tokens defined once in global CSS via `@theme` (e.g. `src/styles/globals.css`). Use token-based classes (`bg-surface-level-2`, `text-text-secondary`), not raw hex values in components.
- No inline `style` except for truly dynamic values (e.g. a progress width). No `!important`. No duplicated CSS.
- Merge conditional classes with a single helper (e.g. `cn()` in `lib/`). Keep styles scoped to the component.
- Shared components get predictable defaults and accept `className` for safe overrides.

## 7. Workflow for every frontend task
1. Inspect the existing implementation first.
2. Find reusable components and patterns before creating new ones.
3. Follow the existing structure and conventions.
4. Keep existing behavior unless a change is asked for.
5. Make the smallest change that does the job.
6. When a shared component changes, check every place that uses it.
7. Compare the result with the Stitch screen (screenshot) before calling it done.
8. Check for duplication and any file over 300 lines.
9. Once the project has them, run lint, type check (`tsc --noEmit`), and build. Report results honestly.
